    "extract": "A fancy girl, sometimes called a fancy maid, was a young woman or girl of African descent with a lighter complexion sold with the intent of forced prostitution and concubinage. This sale was often referred to as the fancy trade within the larger history of slavery in the United States. At least one American slave trader also advertised fancy boys for sale.",
    "extract_html": "<p>A <b>fancy girl</b>, sometimes called a <b>fancy maid</b>, was a young woman or girl of African descent with a lighter complexion sold with the intent of forced prostitution and concubinage. This sale was often referred to as the <b>fancy trade</b> within the larger history of slavery in the United States. At least one American slave trader also advertised <b>fancy boys</b> for sale.</p>"
